   "text": "This is my reading of the drawing as a macrocyclic HCV NS3 protease inhibitor-type structure. I'm unsure of two things: the chain length in the macrocycle and some of the stereodescriptors.\n\n**Fragments read from the image**\n- **Aryl ether:** a 7-methoxy-3-(trifluoromethyl)quinoxalin-2-yl group attached through oxygen to C4 of the pyrrolidine.\n- **Proline core:** the pyrrolidine nitrogen is acylated by the C=O of the amino-acid unit, and its C2 carries a C(=O)NH amide.\n- **Carbamate:** the amino acid's NH is part of an O-(1-cyclopropylethyl) carbamate.\n- **Macrocycle:** the amino acid \u03b1-carbon continues through a chain of CH2 groups to a cis CH=CH. That alkene attaches to a cyclopropane carbon, and the adjacent quaternary cyclopropane carbon bears the NH that closes the ring onto the proline amide.\n- **Sulfonamide:** the quaternary cyclopropane carbon also carries C(=O)NH\u2013SO2\u2013(1-methylcyclopropyl).\n\n**Uncertain points**\n- I counted six CH2 groups in the macrocycle chain, but the drawing is hard to count there.\n- I assigned the proline centres from the usual L-proline and trans-4-substituted pattern (2S,4R) and checked the SMILES descriptors against that.\n- The \u03b1-carbon is assigned as S, an L-amino acid, on the same basis.\n- The cyclopropane centres and the cyclopropylethyl carbon are my best guess rather than a clear reading of the wedges.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H](C1CC1)OC(=O)N[C@H]2CCCCCC/C=C\\[C@@H]3C[C@]3(NC(=O)[C@@H]4C[C@H](Oc5nc6cc(OC)ccc6nc5C(F)(F)F)CN4C2=O)C(=O)NS(=O)(=O)C7(C)CC7"
